    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/CodeZeno/Claude-Code-Usage-Monitor/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>claude code usage monitor taskbar widget windows portable</tags>
    <summary>Windows taskbar widget for monitoring AI coding assistant usage.</summary>
    <description>Claude Code Usage Monitor displays usage limits and reset times for Claude Code, Codex, Google Antigravity, OpenCode Go, Cursor, Grok Build, and GitHub Copilot.

Requires Windows 10 or 11 x64, or Windows 11 on Arm (through x64 emulation), and an installed, signed-in supported provider. No provider software or credentials are included.

Run claude-code-usage-monitor to start the widget, or claude-code-usage-monitor --dashboard for settings and Theme Studio. Save your work and quit both the monitor and dashboard before upgrading or uninstalling. Updates are managed by Chocolatey. Settings are preserved on uninstall.</description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/CodeZeno/Claude-Code-Usage-Monitor/releases/tag/v__VERSION__</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
